  "jobTitle": "Editor / Writer  / Researcher / Web Developer",
  "summary": "I am currently working as a freelance editor and writer, including editorial work for the Charlesworth Group, editing academic papers for journal submissions (psychology, AI, ICT and humanities). I have a particular interest in the environment, science and technology. Since 2010, most of my work has been tied to the Internet, with SEO, SEM and website development being a major concern. I also write fiction and am currently working on a collection of short stories.\n\nPrevious work (prior to 2010) includes editorial and proofreading work for Merlin Unwin Books, a publisher of books on countryside matters. Research projects have included an investigation into the applications of IT to the teaching of writing in higher education (for the Writing & Publishing Set at Middlesex University) and work on a knowledge-based picture interpretation system, developing low-level algorithms written in the C programming language (a cognitive science project at Loughborough University, funded by the Science & Engineering Research Council). In yet another incarnation, I worked for ten years in various capacities in the film, video and TV industry.",
